            "id": "action_5_lonepair_effects"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "action_5_lonepair_effects",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Why Lone Pairs Compress Bond Angles",
          "description": "Examine methane, ammonia, and water side by side. Lone pairs occupy more angular space than bonding pairs, so bond angles decrease from 109.5\u00b0 to 107\u00b0 to 104.5\u00b0."
        },
        "enter": {
