      {
        "id": "action_7_recap",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Recap and Review",
          "description": "Review the key ideas: electron domains repel to maximize separation, steric number sets the electron-domain geometry, lone pairs change molecular geometry, and lone pairs compress bond angles. Use these steps to predict structures from Lewis diagrams."
